//! D236 regression: hex RT fields read from MFEM VisIt data collections must
//! be evaluated with the **nodal GaussLegendre** open basis — the element
//! `RT_FECollection(p, dim)` builds by default (`fem/fe_coll.hpp`,
//! `ob_type = BasisType::GaussLegendre`) and therefore the flavour every
//! MFEM-saved RT coefficient vector lives in — *not* the IntegratedGLL pair
//! (`HexRTk::new`), which is the LOR-only basis of MFEM `fem/lor/lor.cpp`.
//!
//! Reference: the round-40 archives `tmp/d225/dc_RT{1,2}` (single hex
//! `1.0 x 1.2 x 0.8`, unit-dof coefficient vectors `f_k` = e_k generated by
//! `tmp/d158/gen_d158_unit.cpp`) and the C++ `tools/get-values` transcripts
//! `tmp/d225/cppnow_RT{1,2}_p2.txt` (MFEM 4.10, physical point
//! `(0.65, 0.84, 0.6)`, fields in `std::map` order).  The round-40 report
//! recorded the IntegratedGLL evaluation as a 36-token (RT1) / 108-token
//! (RT2) residual against these transcripts; this test pins the
//! GaussLegendre evaluation to the same transcripts.
//!
//! The evaluation below is the get-values pipeline itself:
//! `find_points` reports `[0,1]^3` reference coordinates (D224, re-anchored by
//! D757 after the D721 hex flip), the basis is evaluated there and transformed
//! with the contravariant Piola map of the `[0,1]` isoparametric frame,
//! `phi = J psi / det J` — exactly
//! `GridFunction::evaluate_vector_at_element`'s H(div) arm.

use fem_element::raviart_thomas::{HexRTk, HexRtOpen};
use fem_element::reference::VectorReferenceElement;
use fem_io::mfem::read_mfem;
use fem_mesh::transformation::find_points;
use fem_space::HDivSpace;

